SACLA ANSI test crashes that are GC-INDEPENDENT logic bugs (not rooting gaps).

Found while resuming the SACLA ansi-tests (bootstrap/sacla/lisp/tests/) after the
bignum + GC-rooting-fixpoint work.  Each crash below was classified by loading the
file with the GC DISABLED:

    BOCL_POISON unset; normal build
    ./sources/bocl --no-init --batch -on-error appease \
        --load bootstrap/sacla/lisp/tests/ansi-tests.lisp \
        -x '(cl::%gc-enable nil)' \
        --load bootstrap/sacla/lisp/tests/<FILE>.lisp \
        -x '(cl::%gc-enable t)' -x '(princ :done)'

A crash that still occurs with the GC disabled is GC-INDEPENDENT — a logic bug,
not a use-after-free.  ( (cl::%gc-enable x) and (cl::%gc-stress n) are diagnostic
primitives added in the rooting-fixpoint slice; see
issues/open/deferred-gc-rooting-longtail.issue. )

Confirmed GC-independent (crash persists with GC off):

  - must-symbol.lisp  — SEGV.  Faults in class_of(object=0x8000) (kernel.c) with a
    CORRUPTED C stack (lldb recovers only frame #0), i.e. a wild Ref ~0x8000 is
    passed to class_of.  Preceding recovered errors: "Undefined function: SET",
    "Unbound variable: *GENSYM-COUNTER*", and repeated "check_class: expected
    STRING got INTEGER".  Suspect a symbol/gensym/symbol-name path that builds a
    bogus object once SET / *GENSYM-COUNTER* are exercised.

  - must-printer.lisp — SEGV with GC off.  Not yet localized; capture with
    lldb -b -o run -o 'bt 20' once it is reduced to a single triggering form.

  - must-cons.lisp    — HANG (infinite loop) with GC off.  Last recovered error
    before the hang: "Undefined function: NSUBST-IF-NOT".  Likely a destructive
    cons operator (NSUBST* family) that loops, or a test that builds a circular
    structure a bocl primitive then traverses unboundedly.

  - must-do.lisp      — HANG with GC off.  Last recovered error: "Unbound
    variable: VAR".  Likely a DO/DO* expansion or a test macro looping.

How to reduce: load the file with BOCL_DBG_LOAD=1 to print each top-level form
(F0,F1,...) as it is evaluated; the last F before the crash/hang is the trigger.
Then minimize that form and fix the underlying primitive/special-form.

These block broad SACLA conformance but are independent of the GC rooting work and
of the bignum engine (bignum loads clean here: 0 arithmetic/overflow skips).
Several are gated on missing features (SET, *GENSYM-COUNTER*, NSUBST-IF-NOT,
&whole, DEFINE-METHOD-COMBINATION) per the project priority order
(&whole, defclass, bignum [done], define-method-combination).
